      "open": [],
      "notes": "Efrima and Peleg call this partitioning; the catalogue's partitioning also fixes, in advance, the $k$ points at which the groups of $n/k$ robots gather. Convergence is Partition$(n,1)$. Checked against the full text.",
      "status": "verified",
      "statement": "Partition$(n,k)$ of Efrima and Peleg: $k$ is given to the robots, every group has exactly $n/k$ robots ($\\lfloor n/k\\rfloor$ or $\\lfloor n/k\\rfloor + 1$ when $k$ does not divide $n$), robots in one group **converge** (for every $\\varepsilon$ they are eventually within $\\varepsilon$ of each other) and groups stay more than $2\\eta$ apart, for some fixed $\\eta > 0$. Robots start at distinct points and can count the robots at a point."
    },
